---
/** Section 1: what happens on which day. The times are the cron lines' (scripts/home-run-setup.sh), which a test holds. */
import { howItWorks } from "../../../generated/how-it-works";
import { cronWhen, inWords } from "../../../lib/how-it-works";
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";

const { schedule, constants, settings } = howItWorks;
const weekly = cronWhen(schedule.weeklyCron);
const midweek = cronWhen(schedule.midweekCron);
const deploy = cronWhen(schedule.deployCron);
const days = ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"];
const gaps = (n: number) => Array.from({ length: n });
const discovery = settings.discoveryCadence === "monthly" ? "the first weekly run of each calendar month" : "every weekly run";
---
<p>Two scheduled runs do the research. A third job rebuilds the site every night, so that the dates on its pages stay right. After Monday's run a second model audits what the run changed, and a person reads what it found.</p>

<Figure scroll="The week, day by day">
  <div class="how-week">
    <div></div>
    {days.map((day) => <div class="how-week-day">{day}</div>)}

    <div class="how-week-lane">Research</div>
    <div class="how-week-item how-tone-plain"><time>{weekly.time}</time><b>Weekly run</b>Reads every source, checks what it read, and judges the picks.</div>
    {gaps(2).map(() => <div class="how-week-gap" />)}
    <div class="how-week-item how-tone-plain"><time>{midweek.time}</time><b>Midweek re-verification</b>Checks the events of the next {inWords(constants.reverifyDays)} days again, and nothing else.</div>
    {gaps(3).map(() => <div class="how-week-gap" />)}

    <div class="how-week-lane">Audit</div>
    <div class="how-week-item how-tone-plain"><b>Audit, after the run</b>A second model reviews what the run added or changed. It changes nothing.</div>
    {gaps(6).map(() => <div class="how-week-gap" />)}

    <div class="how-week-lane">By hand</div>
    <div class="how-week-item how-tone-hand"><b>The audit's findings</b>read, with the run's report.</div>
    <div class="how-week-item how-tone-hand" style="grid-column: span 6"><b>Any day</b>Corrections from readers looked into; edits to the rules, the source list and the venue table; a pick made or dropped by hand.</div>

    <div class="how-week-lane">Site</div>
    <div class="how-week-item how-tone-plain" style="grid-column: span 7"><time>{deploy.time}, {deploy.days}</time><b>Nightly rebuild</b>Every page is built again as of the new day, so that "today" is today. A run or an edit by hand also rebuilds the site, within minutes.</div>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">All times are Central. Discovery, the search for events on sites the source list does not cover, runs with {discovery}.</Fragment>
</Figure>
